@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The command is the result; where the machine kept its files is not, and a public repository should not carry either the username or the layout." }
~ Take the home directory out of the published results and the docs

The command is the result; where the machine kept its files is not, and a public repository should not carry either the username or the layout.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "rust-version = \"1.86\"" }
~ Set MSRV to Rust 1.86

To ensure compatibility with dependencies that require newer versions of Rust.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-3 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "homepage     = \"https://github.com/vulogov/rust_smysl\"\nkeywords     = [\"cargo-subcommand\", \"rationale\", \"provenance\", \"smysl\", \"decisions\"]\ncategories   = [\"development-tools::cargo-plugins\", \"development-tools\"]" }
~ Add homepage, keywords, categories, and README to each crate

To provide necessary metadata for crates.io listing and discovery.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "crates.io resolves path dependencies by version, so git, facts and corpus go first, then bench and extract, then verdict and evidence, then the subcommand." }
~ Publish eight crates in a specific order

To ensure path dependencies are resolved correctly by crates.io.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo-smysl` keeps its own keywords rather than the workspace's: it is the crate people install, and they find it by searching for a cargo subcommand." }
~ Keep `cargo-smysl` keywords separate from the workspace

`cargo-smysl` is the crate people install, and they find it by searching for a cargo subcommand.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It also records what to be sure of before publishing, since a version can be yanked but never removed, and a crate name is claimed on first publish." }
~ Document the release process in `docs/releasing.md`

To provide clear instructions for maintaining and publishing the project.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Eight crates publish; the evaluation tooling does not, and says so." }
~ Exclude `cargo-smysl-eval` from publication

`cargo-smysl-eval` is evaluation tooling that reads files outside its own package.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Model-free and self-contained (plan §1): git objects are read with gix, never by running `git`." }
~ Use `gix` for reading git objects instead of running `git`

To ensure self-contained operation without relying on external binaries.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Label and adjudication files are TOML: a person edits them by hand, so they are not JSON." }
~ Pin dependencies to specific versions in the workspace

To maintain consistency across all crates in the workspace.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Hosted providers need TLS; the default build has no network stack at all (D18)." }
~ Add `hosted` feature to some crates for optional TLS support

To provide flexibility in network requirements.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Label and adjudication files are TOML: a person edits them by hand, so they are not JSON." }
~ Use `serde_json` and `toml` for configuration files

To support human-editable configuration files.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/2b514c5b163a.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A published package cannot reach outside itself, so the crate-level README is short and the full documentation stays in the repository." }
~ Include `README.md` in each crate for crates.io listing

To provide brief descriptions for each crate on crates.io.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Whatever becomes a body is now joined into one paragraph, in the one place a body is chosen rather than at each call site" }
~ Do not lose a commit's extraction to a blank line in a quote

Refusing the whole commit for a blank line throws away work that has already been paid for.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "Answering \"why is this like this?\" was dropped as a product claim." }
~ Drop the claim of answering 'why is this like this?' as a product feature

To focus on the tool's actual capabilities rather than unmet claims.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only." }
~ Assign labels, sources and statuses; the model proposes wording only

To maintain control over the integrity of recorded information.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Staleness is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is." }
~ Detect staleness by item body hash rather than line ranges

To accurately track changes in code identity rather than just line positions.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Review as records. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting writes a withdrawal whose reason unit says why, closing writes a resolution." }
~ Record review as confirmations, withdrawals with reasons, and closures with notes

To keep a comprehensive log of all reviews and decisions made.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It ships its own instrument. `bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from." }
~ Ship its own instrument for benchmarking the model

To provide users with the ability to measure the performance of their chosen models on their own commits.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Two thirds of the commands never call a model. Those are the ones worth your time today: they are deterministic, tested, and cost nothing to run." }
~ Focus on deterministic commands over model-dependent ones

To prioritize commands that are reliable, tested, and cost-effective to run.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The figures are published, naming the model each came from, including the experiments that failed." }
~ Publish figures naming the model each came from, including failed experiments

To provide transparency about which models were tested and their results, including any failures.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Over-production is the failure mode that matters. }
~ Highlight over-production as the failure mode that matters

To emphasize the importance of avoiding unnecessary or excessive output in the tool's operations.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The hook only queues and `--estimate` prices a run before it starts. }
~ Meaningfully price extraction runs before starting them

To inform users about the cost of extraction runs before they start, allowing them to make informed decisions.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. }
~ Label cloned corpora as someone else's claims

To clarify the status of units in cloned corpora, indicating that they are not the tool's own claims.

@decision d/ge86482fa7f55-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/bd1f04710855.smy@e86482fa7f55 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Research the truncated-change problem before building for it }
~ Research the truncated-change problem before building for it

The commit message states that research was done to understand the truncated-change problem, which is a significant issue affecting 59% of held-out changes.

